From 059a9cea3acd80c6900384e9fb9630f9444bc847 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mritunjay Sharma <mritunjay.sharma@chainguard.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:36:56 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] crt: build s2n against the shared libcrypto

When aws-crt-python is built with AWS_CRT_BUILD_USE_SYSTEM_LIBCRYPTO=1,
s2n is prebuilt with BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF, so its Findcrypto module
picks the static /usr/lib/libcrypto.a. OpenSSL 4.0's static libcrypto
references brotli (Libs.private: -lbrotlienc -lbrotlidec
-lbrotlicommon), which s2n's try_compile feature probes do not link, so
S2N_LIBCRYPTO_SANITY_PROBE and every other libcrypto probe fail. s2n
then disables features such as HKDF, RSA-PSS signing and providers, and
falls back to ASN1_STRING_data(), which OpenSSL 4.0 removed.

Pass -DS2N_USE_CRYPTO_SHARED_LIBS=ON so s2n uses libcrypto.so. The
awscrt extension already links the shared libcrypto, so its linkage is
unchanged, and the detected libcrypto features match the OpenSSL 3.6
build apart from CONST_X509_GETTERS (new in 4.0) and ENGINE (removed
in 4.0).

Upstream: not submitted (specific to building against a system
OpenSSL 4.0 whose static libcrypto depends on brotli). Chainguard-authored.
---
 crt/CMakeLists.txt | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crt/CMakeLists.txt b/crt/CMakeLists.txt
index 9e32b5a..5014770 100644
--- a/crt/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/crt/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -89,6 +89,11 @@ if(UNIX)
             # headers instead of the bundled aws-lc headers. Not needed on ARM where Homebrew
             # uses /opt/homebrew (not in default search paths), but harmless to set everywhere.
             -DCMAKE_NO_SYSTEM_FROM_IMPORTED=ON
+            # Link s2n and its libcrypto feature probes against the shared
+            # libcrypto. The static libcrypto.a from OpenSSL 4.0 needs brotli at
+            # link time, which the probes do not pass, so every libcrypto probe
+            # fails and s2n silently falls back to its least capable code paths.
+            -DS2N_USE_CRYPTO_SHARED_LIBS=ON
     )
 endif()
 
